From 00521d9ca649b7250f08855b1722b691391a3d19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvia420-bit <salvia420@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:39:41 -0330
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Vehicles (holtburger fork): the high band, the bail-out
 pose, film properties, map-edge unseat fix

Flight experience (2026-11-01/02), every behaviour behind a property that defaults off:
- vehicle_ceiling_agl / vehicle_climb_max applied at spawn (the 5,000 m AGL high band);
  vehicle_derelict_high_agl: an empty vehicle high up despawns 30 s after it went derelict;
  vehicle_high_band_agl: a pilot above it sees by 3D distance (ObjectMaint.Sight3D) and skips
  the monster-awareness checks.
- FlightModel.WorldMax: 255 landblocks (0xFF does not exist).
- vehicle_fall_motion: a bailed-out body is broadcast in retail's Falling motion; a teleport
  during a fall sends the faller a placement-less Touchdown.
- vehicle_gun_players: the gun also hits players on foot, through Player.TakeDamage's own path
  (lifestone protection, death, corpse); never the pilot, a seated or a falling player.
- vehicle_observer_sight_radius: a capable client on foot gets a wider first-sight radius
  (landmarks only beyond 112.5 m), restored on unseat.
- Fix: Unseat clamps the body's placement to landblocks 1-253. A pilot logging out from a
  vehicle drifted into the map's north-east corner put the body in landblock (254, 254), whose
  adjacents ACE cannot load (LandblockManager.GetLandblock IndexOutOfRange took the world
  thread down).

Vehicle tests: 9/9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
